  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Cool mornings and pleasant afternoons the rest of the week.\n\n-  Gusty winds and choppy lakes on Saturday, especially across\n   northwest MT.\n\n-  Pattern shift early next week, gradually cooling with scattered\n   showers.\n\nA ridge of high pressure will bring mostly sunny skies and pleasant\nmid-October weather across the region through Friday, aside from some\npatchy valley fog Friday morning. High temperatures on Friday may stay\nslightly cooler in the valleys than initially expected due to stable\nconditions and cold air trapped in the valleys overnight\n(inversions).\n\nThe pattern shifts this weekend, as a dry cold front sweeps through western\nMontana and north-central Idaho Saturday afternoon and evening. Ahead of\nthe front, breezy westerly winds will help warm daytime temperatures.\nExpect wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph, with exposed higher terrain seeing gusts\nin excess of 50 mph. These winds will create choppy conditions on local\nlakes and pose hazards for small watercraft, especially along the eastern\nshores of Flathead Lake. While a few light showers may pass through\nnorthwest Montana, little to no rain is expected. Afternoon temperatures\nwill remain 5 to 10 degrees above normal for this time of year through\nmid-week.\n\nA broader weather system will move into the western US mid-week. Most of\nthe moisture and storm energy are expected to track well south of our area\ninto the Great Basin. However, the Northern Rockies will still transition\nto a more active weather pattern. Expect a return of showers and a cooldown\nto near-average seasonal temperatures through the end of the week.",
